---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Leow Kah Man | Software Architect & Engineering Leader"
  description="Executive background, architectural philosophy, and engineering leadership perspectives of Leow Kah Man."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12">
    <!-- Hero Intro -->
    <header class="border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pb-10">
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center sm:items-start gap-8">
        <div class="w-28 h-28 sm:w-32 sm:h-32 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900 text-white flex-shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-4xl tracking-tighter shadow-md border-2 border-brand-500/30">
          KM
        </div>
        <div class="flex-1 text-center sm:text-left space-y-4">
          <div class="inline-flex items-center px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-brand-50 text-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-950 dark:text-brand-300 border border-brand-200/60 dark:border-brand-800/60">
            Software Architect &amp; Engineering Leader
          </div>
          <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white leading-tight">
            Leow Kah Man
          </h1>
          <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
            Passionate about architecting cloud platforms, low-overhead distributed systems, and edge infrastructure that scale reliably while minimizing operational complexity.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Bio & Perspective -->
    <section class="prose-tech space-y-6">
      <h2>Engineering Leadership &amp; Philosophy</h2>
      <p>
        I have spent over a decade designing and implementing mission-critical software systems, cloud architectures, and specialized networking infrastructure. My career spans full-stack engineering, distributed systems architecture, and engineering leadership across high-growth product ecosystems.
      </p>
      <p>
        My technical approach is rooted in <strong>engineering pragmatism</strong>: prioritizing proven, high-performance, and verifiable primitives (such as Go, Linux kernel network fastpaths, and zero-JS static edge delivery) over speculative hype cycles. I believe that sustainable software architecture is defined by how gracefully a system handles failure, how cleanly its cognitive load is managed, and how predictably it runs under cost and resource constraints.
      </p>

      <h2>Core Architectural Tenets</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-8 not-prose">
        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 shadow-sm">
          <div class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 font-bold text-lg mb-2">
            1. Zero Trust &amp; Origin Defense
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            Perimeter defense must be multi-layered. Combining Layer 3/4 packet-level ingress filtering with Layer 7 mutual TLS (mTLS) guarantees origins remain cloaked against bypass attacks.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 shadow-sm">
          <div class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 font-bold text-lg mb-2">
            2. Low Cognitive Load &amp; Clean Code
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            Code is read far more often than it is written. Decomposing monolithic routines into composable, self-documenting pipelines is the cornerstone of sustainable team velocity.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 shadow-sm">
          <div class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 font-bold text-lg mb-2">
            3. The Edge as an R&amp;D Engine
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            Running hands-on homelab clusters (K3s, custom DNS, flow-offloaded routers) directly informs disciplined cloud cost management, capacity planning, and failure-mode analysis.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 shadow-sm">
          <div class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 font-bold text-lg mb-2">
            4. Deterministic CI/CD Sandboxing
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            Fast, reproducible pipelines require containerized, isolated build environments with local layer caching, eliminating shared runner wait times and configuration drift.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Get in Touch</h2>
      <p>
        I welcome discussions regarding engineering leadership, technical advisory, distributed systems architecture, and high-performance infrastructure.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Executive Contact / LinkedIn Banner -->
    <div class="p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-slate-900 to-slate-800 text-white shadow-lg border border-slate-700/60 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6">
      <div class="space-y-2 text-center md:text-left">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">
          Connect
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm max-w-lg leading-relaxed">
          For executive networking, advisory, or engineering discussions, reach out on LinkedIn.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center gap-3">
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kmleow"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-500 text-white font-semibold text-sm transition-all shadow-md hover:shadow-lg focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-400"
        >
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 fill-current mr-2.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path d="M19 0h-14c-2.761 0-5 2.239-5 5v14c0 2.761 2.239 5 5 5h14c2.762 0 5-2.239 5-5v-14c0-2.761-2.238-5-5-5zm-11 19h-3v-11h3v11zm-1.5-12.268c-.966 0-1.75-.79-1.75-1.764s.784-1.764 1.75-1.764 1.75.79 1.75 1.764-.783 1.764-1.75 1.764zm13.5 12.268h-3v-5.604c0-3.368-4-3.113-4 0v5.604h-3v-11h3v1.765c1.396-2.586 7-2.777 7 2.476v6.759z"/>
          </svg>
          LinkedIn
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://github.com/kmleow"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-200 border border-slate-600 font-semibold text-sm transition-all shadow-sm"
        >
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 fill-current mr-2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path d="M12 0c-6.626 0-12 5.373-12 12 0 5.302 3.438 9.8 8.207 11.387.599.111.793-.261.793-.577v-2.234c-3.338.726-4.033-1.416-4.033-1.416-.546-1.387-1.333-1.756-1.333-1.756-1.089-.745.083-.729.083-.729 1.205.084 1.839 1.237 1.839 1.237 1.07 1.834 2.807 1.304 3.492.997.107-.775.418-1.305.762-1.604-2.665-.305-5.467-1.334-5.467-5.931 0-1.311.469-2.381 1.236-3.221-.124-.303-.535-1.524.117-3.176 0 0 1.008-.322 3.301 1.23.957-.266 1.983-.399 3.003-.404 1.02.005 2.047.138 3.006.404 2.291-1.552 3.297-1.23 3.297-1.23.653 1.653.242 2.874.118 3.176.77.84 1.235 1.911 1.235 3.221 0 4.609-2.807 5.624-5.479 5.921.43.372.823 1.102.823 2.222v3.293c0 .319.192.694.801.576 4.765-1.589 8.199-6.086 8.199-11.386 0-6.627-5.373-12-12-12z"/>
          </svg>
          GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
